WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.100
Fusion looks like a recipe system.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:06.650
The safer way to read it is as a live decision screen.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:13.400
The developer says Fusion combines two chickens into a mutated monster.

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:16.400
Recorded gameplay shows this route:

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.900
Open Flock, select a chicken, choose Fuse,

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:22.000
then select a second chicken.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.600
Before any confirmation, read the cost displayed on your screen.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:30.000
That number is evidence on that screen;

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.700
this video does not claim a fixed price.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:37.300
One recorded route shows two roles: base and donor,

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:41.100
a lockable trait field, and a result preview.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.700
Those are observed interface elements, not a permanent recipe,

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.700
and may not describe every version.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:51.000
Pause and verify four things you can actually see:

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.300
the first chicken, the second chicken,

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:57.500
the displayed cost, and the full preview.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.400
Do not turn one recording into a rule.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:04.100
No recipe, mutation odds, unlock requirement,

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:07.200
or input-consumption rule is verified here.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.800
Use your live Fuse screen,

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:12.350
then check the evidence notes at Game Hint Lab.
